# The neutral stand-in (Engine v2 E11, #2782): the clip a gesture is drawn as when the agent names none. A stand-in
# is a move (B2, v2/crates/replica/src/moves.rs) named by its clip; it claims what the clip moves and lasts as long.
# A gesture is the body's own move: its contact point is the body's root, so it reaches nothing else.
{
  1: "Idle", 2: 1,
  3: [{1: 2, 2: 3}],                        # claims the gaze
  5: [3],
  6: [{1: "souls:start-up", 2: 300000}, {1: "souls:hold", 2: 1700000}],
  7: {1: 1},
  8: 1,
  9: "souls:root"
}
